docs: unbloat How Agentic Workflows Work blog post (#11890)

Reduced from 582 to 246 lines (57.7% reduction, 336 lines removed).

Changes:
- Condensed frontmatter configuration section from excessive bullet lists into concise prose
- Shortened "Effective prompts" from 8 bullets to a single sentence
- Streamlined compilation process details (schema validation, security, imports, job generation)
- Consolidated agent execution environment from 3 separate lists into one paragraph
- Reduced output types examples from 5 detailed code blocks to 2 representative examples
- Compressed auditable artifacts from 4 detailed sections into one paragraph
- Unified AI engine interface from 4 verbose sections into one concise paragraph with single code example
- Simplified MCP server architecture from 3 sections to 1 paragraph
- Condensed error handling and debugging from 4 sections to 1 paragraph
- Reduced performance considerations from 3 sections with multiple bullets to 2 sentences

All essential information preserved while significantly improving scannability and reducing cognitive load.

